        <body>
            <div xml:id="d419">

                <pb facs="0903" n="819" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg819"/>

                <head>No. 414.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Curry to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-10-26"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 26, 1886</date>.
                        (Received November 9.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 138.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of the history of the
                    agreement of February 13, 1884, I inclose a note of the minister of state, in
                    the original text and a translation, together with my proposition for a new
                    agreement. It will be observed that I was seeking to get rid of the present
                    agreement, unquestionably ambiguous in its phraseology, and of the complications
                    which render it’ partially nugatory so far as benefit to the United States is
                    concerned, and a hindrance to a wider and more satisfactory engagement. The
                    trade in American vessels between foreign ports and the ports of Cuba and Porto
                    Rico was omitted to avoid troublesome demands by foreign Governments, and
                    because this feature of our commerce had not been specially emphasized in recent
                    instructions.</p>
                <p>Nothing has come of the propositions, as the revocation of the proclamation of
                    February 14, 1884, has given a new phase to the whole discussion.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. L. M. CURRY.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d419-a1.xml" xpointer="d419-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
